Terminals unused in grammar

    SEMICOLON
    DOT


Grammar

    0 $accept: program $end

    1 program: package_decl import_decl declaration_list func_decl
    2        | package_decl declaration_list func_decl

    3 package_decl: PACKAGE IDENTIFIER

    4 import_decl: IMPORT STRING_LITERAL

    5 declaration_list: ε
    6                 | declaration_list declaration

    7 declaration: var_decl

    8 var_decl: VAR IDENTIFIER INT

    9 func_decl: FUNC IDENTIFIER LPAREN RPAREN LBRACE func_body RBRACE

   10 func_body: local_decl_list statement_list

   11 local_decl_list: ε
   12                | local_decl_list var_decl

   13 statement_list: ε
   14               | statement_list statement

   15 statement: assignment_stmt
   16          | return_stmt
   17          | scanf_stmt
   18          | printf_stmt
   19          | block_stmt

   20 assignment_stmt: IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expression

   21 return_stmt: RETURN expression

   22 scanf_stmt: FMT_SCANF LPAREN format_string COMMA var_list RPAREN

   23 printf_stmt: FMT_PRINTF LPAREN format_string RPAREN
   24            | FMT_PRINTF LPAREN format_string COMMA arg_list RPAREN

   25 block_stmt: LBRACE statement_list RBRACE

   26 format_string: STRING_LITERAL

   27 var_list: AMPERSAND IDENTIFIER
   28         | var_list COMMA AMPERSAND IDENTIFIER

   29 arg_list: expression
   30         | arg_list COMMA expression

   31 expression: additive

   32 additive: multiplicative
   33         | additive PLUS multiplicative
   34         | additive MINUS multiplicative

   35 multiplicative: unary
   36               | multiplicative STAR unary
   37               | multiplicative SLASH unary
   38               | multiplicative PERCENT unary

   39 unary: primary
   40      | MINUS unary
   41      | AMPERSAND unary

   42 primary: IDENTIFIER
   43        | INTEGER_CONST
   44        | LPAREN expression RPAREN


